```markdown
# PR155 exact-final-head hosted audit

All relevant started runs reached terminal outcomes at published HEAD `fee364c6d61a5feebf08dbdd830a5a57ee2d872b`, tree `ace7e44cd89194d189a30a0aa6cf513a45b3b87c`. Actual hosted checkout `90e222635a01e89f095e9a256ac69ecfc759ec4e` has ordered parents frozen154 `91827360c185cbf813277bf32a6627d894b1b20a` and this feature. The API commit, every receipt and run metadata agree; effective checkout and feature trees match. No final Git mutation or workflow dispatch/rerun/cancellation was performed by this support audit.

| Final run | Terminal | Actual validation |
|---|---|---|
| [Development40006927076](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/40006927076) | SUCCESS | `development_checks_passed`, `full_acceptance=false`;0 product pytest/232 required-unexecuted files. Static, smoke and schema checks pass. Separate policy infrastructure unittests31+4 PASS. |
| [Access40006927148](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/40006927148) | FAILURE | Main2786:2487PASS/279FAIL/20ERROR. Broad3148:2849PASS/279FAIL/20ERROR. Zero skip in both. Main entirely inside broad, so Access product-lane unique ordinary union3148; never summed. |
| [Pages40006927071](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/40006927071) | SUCCESS |8 documentation tests PASS; deployment job and production Pages configuration/upload skipped. Preview artifact uploaded. |

The actual final **Access product-lane** union omits3349 of the same-input6497 ordinary source nodes, across143 files. This scope excludes the separately reported Pages documentation8, policy31 and CI runtime4 ancillary cases; it is not an all-workflow union or combined product-acceptance claim. All154 newly added integration nodes remain omitted from the Access product lanes. Main collected.txt equals its actual JUnit identities. Exact node/file lists are in `hosted-node-union.json`; the reviewed passing README node/assertion replacement remains separately mapped in the initial audit.

Separate source I4(217)/I5(29) and each fresh direct/derived installed I4(217)/I5(29) PASS. Installed I2/I3 probes, runtime/import bindings, complete wheel/metadata/RECORD comparisons pass. Both original Access smokes in the I5 driver exit1, and both separate distribution smokes exit1 with empty stdout and `AdmissionRefused: PERMISSION_DENIED` at installed `application/exchange.py:397`. Both wheel SHA256 values are `2452e419e06eea774805fc89358130538c50fdd313fdb0fb9b82b230e99a39d8`. These are preserved I6-C boundary refusals, not Transfer activation or whole-product acceptance.

Access failed main runtime, broad orchestrator, old79 comparator, installed orchestrator, original distribution smoke verifier and acceptance-ledger reconciliation. Evidence, formatting, final runtime audit, receipt emission and upload continued. The old comparator honestly reports baseline79/current299, resolved0/additional220, same_nodes=false; this is a separate historical scope, not a regression comparison against154.

## Exact final receipts

- Development: **86002 bytes**, SHA256 `9449cf850e69b9922fc8604f308d63f370e9b8df599e60ded74f823ae90a895c`, all**21 indexed payloads** independently verified.
- Access: **1993958 bytes**, SHA256 `60b73fee0f3fed6d0c220d94a5fb62b450ad18bbb2ff58c662bb3f9bee3b090a`, all**123 indexed payloads** independently verified.

Both have exact BEGIN/DATA/END, strict base64, closed-ZIP byte length/SHA256, matching END digest, unique members, complete index sizes/hashes and actual run/checkout/tree binding. The final Access log again contains exactly one line-leading BOM-prefixed receipt record, accepted by the previously counterchecked strict parser. Payload bytes were not repaired or stripped. Both receipts are below2097152; **actual hosted overflow was not exercised** on this final tree.

Fresh source6497/6198PASS/279FAIL/20ERROR versus each actual final hosted main/broad invocation: exactly299 non-success identities; all phases, outcomes, primary messages and typed-refusal token sets match. Each source exception short name occurs in hosted rendered messages/tracebacks299/299. Full rendered messages match280/299 and rendered project-frame projections135/299; raw traceback text differs. Hosted actual ExceptionInfo and reached-assertion sidecars are absent, so actual hosted frame-function, exception-object or assertion-reach equality cannot be inferred. The parent's independently recorded source-side diagnostic remains separate. Raw rendered entries and actual source exceptions are retained in compressed comparison evidence.

## Three distinct input contracts

Independent `input-invariance493.json` verifies all493 tested execution/distribution file bytes, lengths, SHA256 and Git blobs equal the final published tree. Only the new evidence directory and22-line skill lesson changed after the tested `fb5d7b5a` tree.

CI's acceptance-input contract is broader: initial `106d274117017ca99caafb07b20c36eed6a9995dfa752f6bebfcfbe047618a67` changes to final `ee1b871e0cd2fde4f24272975ada0c0da4a2ac32d6b8ba2511de6b356831d1e1`. Both hashes independently recompute from the exact Git trees and equal their actual plans/manifests. Its input set grows8646→9295 via649 new unclassified evidence paths, with zero changed-existing or removed CI inputs. **No unchanged-CI-hash claim is made.**

The distribution source inventory independently remains `38592a0e30468a80e442ee35d514673beace31eb98daf5cfda1109ac1675d4ed` for163 source/build metadata files, including160 product files. Final Development's sync planner marks lightweight sdist preparation not_applicable; it did not rerun that gate. Final Access independently rebuilds and validates the same sdist:702494 compressed bytes,6041897 regular bytes,164 members,6174720 tar-stream bytes; SHA256 `9d228f889f9507cdc5a166b9658e80873fcbd48255c6c958eb90e33954014b54`. Every member/source hash and full wheel equivalence remain in the verified receipt.

Hosted product Python3.12.15 loads its environment SQLite3.53.1/source ID `2026-05-05 10:34:17 c88b22011a54b4f6fbd149e9f8e4de77658ce58143a1af0e3785e4e6475127e9`. No SQLite component was downloaded/built/replaced by this audit.

## Artifacts and access limits

Actual upload logs agree with final API metadata:

| Artifact | Bytes | Published SHA256 |
|---|---:|---|
| Development12523848713 |85791|`ebc0bec2532dbd3c57d87154ce4bb6e04ce62a5f011fe773a90fd58c8905eb92`|
| Access12524818073 |856700515|`ca97a1db8fff294fad2d5d4be893e3f4338a9737381a17a9010ac1efc9a33872`|
| Pages12523659234 |4576208|`9372b12886c29f5c813f3daf5768be1101b064f4862e78d5e0318ea66b1355d9`|

Final artifact binary downloads were **not attempted** because all three initial artifact reads had established Azure Forbidden/zero-byte access limits. Previously denied targets were not retried. These final artifacts were not newly denied and no downloaded-byte/hash verification or download success is claimed. Supported plugin job logs and API metadata succeeded; indexed log receipts were independently verified. Actual upload succeeded, actual hosted overflow and successful artifact download remain unexecuted.

Audit corrections are retained externally: a visual double-escape suspicion was disproved by actual skill bytes (7 backslashes,0 double pairs), positive matches and equality to the executed parser; no skill change was needed. A verifier initially expected a final Development sdist member and failed KeyError; it now handles the actual not_applicable scope, retaining the initial helper/log. These are audit-harness corrections, not product failures or reruns.

No remaining CI run is pending. Development success is not Release acceptance. No main merge, Release workflow, deployment, product change or final binary-download retry occurred. This final audit stays external to avoid self-referential Git-tree evidence; `ARTIFACTS.json` binds its payloads. Final PR description/handoff should cite these exact run URLs, receipt hashes and limits.

Editorial clarification: Access product-lane union/omission labels were clarified after delivery; counts, underlying receipts and run outcomes are unchanged. Previous external report/summary/index snapshots are retained under `editorial-prior/`. Ancillary workflow counts remain separate. No repository mutation or CI/test rerun was performed.

